# Validation example: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, SCF_DIRECT_4C TRUE + CHOLESKY FALSE (dense) +
# FUNCTIONAL_DIRECT_4C TRUE + FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE -- confirms SCF_DIRECT_4C no longer
# forces the Cholesky route downstream: the SCF loop is integral-direct, but the post-SCF
# positive-energy AND untrimmed (MINMAX) MO integrals come from the dense path
# (buildC4SpinorEri + rkbMoTwoElectronSymmetric), exactly as CHOLESKY FALSE alone would build
# them. FUNCTIONAL_DIRECT_4C TRUE is a harmless no-op here (dense already avoids RkbCholesky).
# Compare the converged energy against lih_gnof_c4_neg_full_optimization.inp's own dense result
# -- must match exactly (same dense construction either way).
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE
SCF_DIRECT_4C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL_DIRECT_4C TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
